<title>Recover your Origin Account</title>
</head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:24px;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;color:#1a1a1a;background:#ffffff">
<div style="max-width:560px;margin:0 auto">
<p>Hello,</p>
<p>SourceOrigin support started a recovery of the Origin Account <strong>@ada</strong>, so its owner can add a new passkey. The account was signed out everywhere. If it is yours, open the link below and follow the steps to add a passkey.</p>
<p>
<a href="https://auth.sourceorigin.dev/recover#token=TOKEN" style="display:inline-block;padding:10px 18px;border-radius:8px;background:#1a1a1a;color:#ffffff;text-decoration:none">Add a passkey</a>
</p>
<p style="font-size:14px;color:#555555">Or copy this link: https://auth.sourceorigin.dev/recover#token=TOKEN</p>
<p>The link works once, for 72 hours. If you didn’t ask for this, contact SourceOrigin support. If you still have a passkey, you can also <a href="https://auth.sourceorigin.dev/recover/undo#recovery=RECOVERY">cancel the recovery</a>.</p>
<p>SourceOrigin</p>
</div>
</body>
</html>
